The earlier version of this section said 444 and 153. Both were true of the tree
they were measured on — `docs/acceptance/LC-P1-14-release-contents.md` records
them at that revision and is left as written — and both are older than
`src/labcairn` grew to 213 files. The counts above are what this revision builds.
An attempt at this measurement earlier in the same day counted 835 sdist members,
and the one extra member was its own untracked `build.log`, written inside the
directory being exported; the export was redone with the log outside it.

The exact member counts for the release as built are in
docs/acceptance/LC-P1-14-release-contents.md. The release workflow re-measures
both lists on every run and fails if either artefact carries a member the
committed tree does not, or is missing one the tree has.

Two things follow, and both are checked by the release workflow rather than
asserted here:

  * No third-party source code is vendored into either artefact. Every member
    is a file of this repository.

  * The runtime dependencies are NOT redistributed in either artefact. The
    wheel's metadata names them (Requires-Dist) and the installer fetches
    each one as its own distribution, under its own licence and carrying its
    own notices. Section 2 is about what arrives that way.

The only third-party files the distribution carries as files are the three
papers in §4.


