2.3  The three that carry a condition, and the four that carry a bundled
     third-party licence of their own
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * MPL-2.0 — certifi (MPL-2.0) and tqdm (MPL-2.0 AND MIT, so MIT is
    available as well). MPL 2.0 is file-level copyleft: it obliges a
    distributor of a modified copy of a covered file to offer that file's
    source under MPL 2.0. Neither package is modified by LabCairn, and
    LabCairn does not redistribute either of them.

  * numpy 2.5.4 — its licence file (numpy-2.5.4.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE.txt)
    carries the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1 for the OpenBLAS build
    statically linked into numpy.libs, stated as
    "GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1". The exception is what makes
    the GPL terms compatible with distribution under other terms.

  * Pillow 13.0.0 — its licence file
    (pillow-13.0.0.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE) carries the FreeType
    licences for the bundled FreeType 2.14.3: "the FreeType License ... or
    the GNU General Public License version 2", offered as two mutually
    exclusive choices. It also carries the brotli 1.2.0 licence and the zlib
    licence.

  * pywin32 312 — Windows-only. Its licence directory carries an LGPL
    notice for the bundled adodbapi module
    (pywin32-312.dist-info/licenses/adodbapi/license.txt) and the Scintilla
    licence for the bundled Scintilla sources
    (pywin32-312.dist-info/licenses/pythonwin/Scintilla/License.txt), beside
    the PSF-licensed pywin32 code itself.

These four are listed because the lesson of this repository is that a
distribution's root licence line is not a statement about everything inside
it: paper-qa's AGPL subpackage was invisible to a root-level check, and the
same is true of a dependency's bundled third-party module.

