an installer's licence *screen* - and misses `emoji-regex@8.0.0`'s
`LICENSE-MIT.txt`.

Two limits on this section, stated rather than assumed:

  * `shell/node_modules` is absent from the checkout. This section is anchored
    to the **lockfile**; whether an installed tree matches it is measured by
    `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, which §5.3 names.
  * The Electron **runtime binary's** embedded inventory is not restated here
    (the paragraph above), and no installed Electron binary was inspected by
    this measurement.

`shell/test/dependency-surface.test.mjs` re-measures the 273 keys against the
approved set in both directions on every run, so a package adopted without being
recorded and a recorded package that left the lock both redden it. Nothing
watched the *licences* on this side until `shell/test/notice-licences.test.mjs`
landed with this section: §5's licence audit resolves the Python closure with
`uv export`, and never reads `shell/`.

